				\begin{document}$${{{{{\rm{\eta }}}}}}=\frac{{hA}\,\varDelta {T}_{\max }-{Q}_{s}}{I(1-{10}^{-{A}_{808}})}$$\end{document}η=hAΔTmax−QsI(1−10−A808)where h is the coefficient of heat transfer, A is the container surface area, ΔT is the temperature change of the solution of SnSNPs@PEG, I is the power density of the NIR laser, A808 is the absorbance of the solution of SnSNPs@PEG at 808 nm, and Qs is the heat associated with the light absorbance of the solution.
